      "article_id": "article_04f1e257b7e0139c",
      "body_recovery_method": "wayback",
      "context_excerpt": "Most AI agents today are triggered by a prompt, complete a defined task and then stop running. A long-running autonomous agent, or “claw,” works differently. These agents run persistently in the background, completing tasks on their own and surfacing only what requires a human decision. They operate on a heartbeat: At regular intervals, they check their task list, evaluate what needs action, and either act or wait for the next cycle.",
